+For the following formula choose a toroidal compactification to which the
+Torelli map extends, and interpret pullbacks in a smooth neighborhood of its
+image, or on a compatible resolution. Arbitrary smooth compactifications
+need not themselves carry an extension from bar(M_g). The second Voronoi or
+perfect-cone compactification supplies the usual extension, with the image
+in its nonsingular locus [S4, Section 1.9]. Equivalently, extend the pullback
+classes from M_g^ct to bar(M_g); lambda_g kills ambiguity supported outside
+compact type. In the displayed formula T^* on extended classes denotes the
+pullback by this compatible extended morphism.
